1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,500
Good afternoon. Welcome to Riverside Public
Library. Have you just moved to the area?

2
00:00:04,875 --> 00:00:07,600
I have, yes.
I'd like to join the library, please.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:10,677
Of course. To join, new
members must show proof of

4
00:00:10,701 --> 00:00:13,972
address, so I'll just need
something like a utility bill.

5
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,320
I've got one right here.

6
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:18,428
Perfect. Now, membership
is free for residents,

7
00:00:18,452 --> 00:00:21,152
so since you live
locally, there's no charge.

8
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:22,720
Oh, that's great to hear.

9
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,900
It does cost a small fee for
non-residents, but that won't apply to you.

10
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:29,580
Good. How many books can I borrow at once?

11
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:32,680
Each member can borrow
up to ten items at a time.

12
00:00:32,845 --> 00:00:35,360
Ten? That's plenty. And for how long?

13
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:38,100
You can keep them for three
weeks before they're due back.

14
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,060
Three weeks. Understood. What
happens if I'm late returning something?

15
00:00:42,345 --> 00:00:45,380
Overdue items incur a
fine of 20 cents per day.

16
00:00:45,645 --> 00:00:49,800
20 cents. Fair enough.
Does the card give access to anything else?

17
00:00:50,189 --> 00:00:53,880
Yes. The library card also gives
access to the library computers.

18
00:00:54,215 --> 00:00:55,215
Oh, useful.

19
00:00:55,449 --> 00:00:57,820
And free Wi-Fi as well, whenever you visit.

20
00:00:58,095 --> 00:00:59,699
Great. I'll definitely use that.

21
00:00:59,723 --> 00:01:02,572
Is there anything special
about children's membership?

22
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,960
Children's membership requires
a parent's signature on the form.

23
00:01:06,235 --> 00:01:09,040
I'll remember that for my daughter.
When is the library open?

24
00:01:09,339 --> 00:01:11,760
We're open every day
except public holidays.

25
00:01:12,134 --> 00:01:16,080
Every day? That's convenient.
Can I renew books without coming in?

26
00:01:16,329 --> 00:01:19,660
Yes. Members can renew books
online through the library's website.

27
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:22,220
That's handy. What if I lose my card?

28
00:01:23,034 --> 00:01:25,060
A lost card can be replaced for $5.

29
00:01:25,649 --> 00:01:28,820
$5. Noted. Do you run any regular events?

30
00:01:29,099 --> 00:01:31,080
We host a monthly book club for adults.

31
00:01:31,339 --> 00:01:32,920
Oh, I might join that.

32
00:01:32,921 --> 00:01:35,660
And a weekly storytime
session for children, too.

33
00:01:36,009 --> 00:01:39,560
My daughter would love that.
Can I book a private space to study?

34
00:01:40,029 --> 00:01:42,220
Study rooms can be
booked for up to two hours.

35
00:01:42,445 --> 00:01:46,440
Two hours? That should be enough. Can I
borrow anything from the reference section?

36
00:01:46,719 --> 00:01:50,400
The reference section cannot be borrowed,
I'm afraid. Those stay in the building.

37
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:53,500
That's fine. Understood.
Do you ever collect donations?

38
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,860
Donations of books are
accepted every Saturday.

39
00:01:57,429 --> 00:01:59,380
Good to know. I've got a few to bring in.

40
00:01:59,979 --> 00:02:01,980
Will I get reminders before books are due?

41
00:02:02,379 --> 00:02:05,600
Members receive email reminders
three days before the due date.

42
00:02:05,869 --> 00:02:08,800
That's very helpful.
Do you have any special open days?

43
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:12,860
The library's annual open day is
held in June, with lots of activities.

44
00:02:13,295 --> 00:02:16,560
I'll look out for that. Is there anything
for me today as a new member?

45
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:19,480
New members receive a free
bookmark to celebrate joining.

46
00:02:19,769 --> 00:02:22,280
Lovely.
Thank you so much for all the information.

47
00:02:22,281 --> 00:02:24,700
You're very welcome. Enjoy the library.

